  "reason": "R1 and R10 establish that empirical EAM/MEAM potentials can have system- and temperature-dependent fidelity in multicomponent refractory alloys and should be checked against DFT, which weakly motivates adopting a more accurate interatomic model. R8 loosely points toward atomic-occupancy effects, while R12 and R17 show the broader importance of including omitted free-energy contributions in phase-stability calculations. However, none of the records proposes a machine-learning MTP, replacing thermodynamic integration with free-energy perturbation, exploiting low MTP–DFT energy-difference variance, or combining electronic DOS and solid-state SRO corrections to predict TaVCrW melting. Thus, the records point generally toward improving potentials and thermodynamic descriptions, but the specific efficient MTP–FEP intervention would require a substantial new idea."
